{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1164949-new-horror-the-invader","id":1164949,"title":"[New Horror] The Invader","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-03T19:32:35-08:00","id":1164949,"title":"[New Horror] The Invader","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/60/01/84/600184bf32bbcd32a7c38ca9ebd51a5f.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">From ancient times to the modern day, mankind has gazed at the stars, wondering if it was alone in the universe and what its brothers from other worlds might be like. The means of attempting communication with such entities have rarely succeeded up until the present, in a military facility in the middle of the desert. Grandiose radio towers were built to send radio signals for years on end, with little to show for it.<br /> <br /> But one fateful day, people started being visited by this strange celestial humanoid in a crystalline suit resembling that of an astronaut. They disappeared without a trace, only to return with vague reports of having their minds and bodies altered by the entity inside an underground complex. So far, all expeditions into this supposed hideout have yielded inconclusive results at best and unexplained loss of talented people at worst. One of those individuals who was abducted tried to leak the stories, and is still on the run from the government.<br /> <br /> As for the entity\u2019s current whereabouts, no one knows. Periodically new stories matching its description show up on the Internet and publications about the paranormal, none ever showing the full picture or really shedding any meaningful light into its origins and motivations. Regardless of efforts from people in high echelons of the government, more people are finding out about the Invader and seeking it out.<br /> <br /> As far as the entity is concerned, all is under control. Its puppets have been embedded everywhere, ready to be activated without them being any wiser. The system has been compromised, and no one is to be trusted. The earthlings are simply acting according to plan.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Enigmatic<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Observant<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Collect Information About The Earth<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 8, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 8, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 6, Composure 6<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Investigation (Spying) 4, Science 6, Stealth (In Plain Sight) 2, Persuasion 4, Subterfuge (False Clues) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Common Sense 3, Iron Will 2, Safe Place 3 (Underground Laboratory), Untouchable 1, Table Turner 1, Aura Reading 3 (Uses Science Instead Of Empathy)<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 16<br /> <b>Defense: </b>10 (Uses Science Instead Of Athletics)<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 14<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15 [Flight 25]<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10 (Size 6)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 6<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Blast (Death Ray) [+0L To +3L, Wits + Science, Maximum Range Of 80 Yards]<br /> <br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot abide sounds of extremely high frequency, which is represented through the Insensate Tilt. It must either flee from or destroy the source of the sound.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> The crystals formed at the landing site of its spaceship.<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Elusive, Numen (Blast, Metamorphosis, Telepathy), Surprise Entrance, Unbreakable, Vanish<br /> <br /> <b>Elusive:</b> Creatures with this Dread Power only ever appear on camera as a blurred silhouette of their actual shape. Humanoid monsters can easily be mistaken for humans or upright bears, while unusually large creatures blend into the scenery. Humans have a hard time remembering exact detail about creatures they encounter. Rolls to accurately describe or recall such events are made at a \u20133 modifier.<br /> <br /> <b>Metamorphosis:</b> When working on an incapacitated or non-resisting living creature, the entity can alter that creature\u2019s physical make up. This Numen requires a Finesse + Resistance roll to activate. Changes such as the targets appearance, race, or gender cost 3 Essence. Other, more substantial, changes may also be made. By spending 5 Essence, the entity can bestow one of the following for each Success:<br /> \u2022 A point of Armor<br /> \u2022 1L of natural weaponry rating<br /> \u2022 A sense that the victim does not normally possess (such as echolocation, infrared vision, or similar)<br /> \u2022 A Dread Power that suits the change in question<br /> <br /> <b>Telepathy:</b> Entities with this Numen can reach out and link their minds with others, allowing instantaneous and reliable communication. This Numen costs one Essence. If the target chooses to resist, the roll is contested by the target\u2019s Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Advantage. Success allows the entity to freely communicate with the target and to read their thoughts until the end of the scene. If the target is mortal, they gain the Shaken Condition - being that intimate with an alien mind is profoundly disturbing.<br /> <br /> <b>Vanish:</b> The Horror with this Dread Power can disappear in a flash, a puff of smoke, or the blink of an eye. Once per scene, by spending 1 Willpower, the creature may instantly exit the scene. The Horror must have an established location (at least a dot in the Safe Place Merit or equivalent) that it retreats to when using this ability.</div></div> </div> </div>","